From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:48:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] let a product turn off free zoom and label lenses by focal
 length

Add the bool config_enableZoom, true by default. When a product sets it
to false, the user can't zoom freely: pinch to zoom does nothing, the
zoom slider never shows, the Zoom action is gone from the settings of
the hardware keys (a stored one is ignored), and tapping the active lens
button does nothing. The lens buttons are the only way to change the
field of view.

Label and order the lens buttons by the ratio of each camera's 35
mm-equivalent focal length (the focal length over the sensor diagonal)
to that of the main camera of its side, instead of the ratio of view
angles that CameraX truncates to whole degrees. The main camera of a
side is the one with the lowest ID, and all the external cameras are
one side. A ratio within 20 % of 0.5, 1, 2, 2.5, 3, 4 or 5 takes that
label, and any other shows one decimal. CameraX's ratio stays the
fallback for a camera whose characteristics lack the focal length or
the sensor size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
